<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Henan</h1><p class="st-meta">206 BCE – 205 BCE · capital Luoyang</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived kingdom around Luoyang, one of Xiang Yu's Eighteen Kingdoms, whose king Shen Yang surrendered to Liu Bang in 205 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu's</a> settlement of 206 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shen-yang">Shen Yang</a>, a former official of Zhao and associate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-er">Zhang Er</a>, was rewarded for welcoming Chu forces at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> by being made King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>, with his capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom held the strategic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> basin, the gateway between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanzhong">Guanzhong</a> region and the eastern plain. It lasted too briefly for any distinctive government to develop.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> emerged from the west in 205 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shen-yang">Shen Yang</a> surrendered without a fight, and his kingdom became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commandery">Commandery</a>. Its loss opened the route east for Liu Bang's ill-fated march on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuzhou">Pengcheng</a>, capital of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/western-chu">Western Chu</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 206 BCE – 205 BCE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:55.60%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>206 BCE – 205 BCE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Luoyang</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Shen Yang</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese ancestral religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Chinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Henan (Shen Yang)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-206&amp;focus=kingdom-of-henan" aria-label="Kingdom of Henan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7535 923 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Henan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7855 1179L7739 1235"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7739 1235h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7855 1179h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7855 1179h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Luoyang. <a href="/atlas?year=-206&amp;focus=kingdom-of-henan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

